@startuml
title Airflow–Spark Integration (Docker Compose)
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
left to right direction

actor "Data Engineer" as User

rectangle "Docker Compose 3.7 Environment" as Compose {
  database "Postgres\n(port 5432)\nAirflow metadata" as PG

  component "Airflow Webserver + Scheduler\n(LocalExecutor)\nHTTP 8282\nPySpark installed" as Airflow

  frame "Spark Standalone Cluster\n(Spark 2.4.5 / Hadoop 2.6)" as SparkCluster {
    component "Spark Master\ncluster: 7077\nUI: 8181\nhostname: spark" as Master
    component "Spark Worker 1" as Worker1
    component "Spark Worker 2" as Worker2
    component "Spark Worker 3" as Worker3
    note right of Worker3
      Additional workers can be added following the same pattern.
    end note
  }

  component "Jupyter / PySpark Notebook\nHTTP 8888\nSpark App UIs 4040-4080" as Jupyter

  folder "DAGs" as DAGs
  folder "Spark Applications" as Apps
  folder "Notebooks" as NB
  folder "Input Data" as Data
}

User --> Airflow : HTTP 8282
User --> Jupyter : HTTP 8888

Airflow --> PG : Metadata (SQL)
Airflow --> Master : Submit Spark apps\nSparkSubmitOperator via 'spark_default'\nspark://spark:7077

Jupyter --> Master : Interactive PySpark jobs

Master --> Worker1 : Dispatch workloads
Master --> Worker2 : Dispatch workloads
Master --> Worker3 : Dispatch workloads
Worker1 --> Master : Register
Worker2 --> Master : Register
Worker3 --> Master : Register

DAGs ..> Airflow : mounted
Apps ..> Airflow : read
Apps ..> Master : read
Apps ..> Worker1 : read
Apps ..> Worker2 : read
Apps ..> Worker3 : read
NB ..> Jupyter : mounted
Data ..> Airflow : read
Data ..> Jupyter : read/write
Data ..> Worker1 : read
Data ..> Worker2 : read
Data ..> Worker3 : read

note right of Airflow
 Uses SparkSubmitOperator
 Connection: spark_default -> spark://spark:7077
 Includes pyspark for in-container spark-submit
end note

note right of Master
 Web UI 8181; cluster endpoint 7077
end note

note bottom of Compose
 Local dev/test only: Spark RPC auth/encryption and SSL disabled
end note

@enduml
